summary: Test case for *_reserve_kbytes check
description: |
    Summary: 
    #bz-1127398
    Allow administrators to control the amount of reserved memory in the kernel

    For overcommit 'guess', we can sum resident set sizes (RSS).
    On x86_64 this is about 8MB.
    	
    #Until now, RHEL6 has not apply this patch
    For overcommit 'never', we can take the max of their virtual sizes (VSZ)
    and add the sum of their RSS.
    On x86_64 this is about 128MB.

contact: Li Wang <liwang@redhat.com>
link:
  - relates: https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=1127398
component:
  - kernel
test: ./runtest.sh
framework: beakerlib
recommend: []
duration: 1m
extra-summary: /kernel/general/memory/function/control-the-reserved-memory
extra-task: /kernel/general/memory/function/control-the-reserved-memory

